# Lock files ARE committed, overriding the global ignore rule.
#
# The wasi module's lock matters most: OutLayer compiles it inside the enclave and attests the
# hash of the resulting wasm, so an unpinned dependency graph means the same source can compile
# to a different binary. It also keeps the build working at all — the worker's compiler image is
# Rust 1.85, and an unpinned resolve pulls icu/idna versions that require 1.86.
#
# The service locks matter for the same reason any deployed binary's do: a rebuild on the host
# should produce what was tested, not whatever crates.io published since.
!Cargo.lock
!wasi-near-email-ark/Cargo.lock
!db-api/Cargo.lock
!smtp-server/Cargo.lock
